node_modules/
# Phase 10C rollback-simulation finding: this was previously unanchored
# ("backups/"), which also matched n8n_workflows/backups/ — a real,
# meaningful artifact (ADR-045's n8n export backup, read by
# mission_control_api.py's _automation()) that was invisible to git as a
# result. Anchored to the repo root so it only excludes the root-level
# CONSTITUTION.md rolling backups it was actually meant for.
/backups/
*.log
.env
# Security P1 C2 (2026-08-18): recovery/snapshot.py's .env snapshot copies
# are full plaintext secret bundles (all API keys). They live beside .env
# at .env.snapshot-<ts>.bak -- unlike data/*.jsonl.snapshot-*.bak (internal
# business data, committed by convention), these must never land in git.
.env.snapshot-*.bak
.factory_loop.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Scratch/manual test-run PDF output at repo root (not demo_cookbook.pdf,
# which book_generator.py's own default demo mode intentionally produces —
# see CLAUDE.md). STRUCTURAL_DIAGNOSIS.md disease #12.
/cookbook_cover.pdf
/cover_test.pdf
/demo.pdf
/healthy_eating_120.pdf
/output.pdf
/test_output.pdf
books/regression_test_draft_with_content.pdf
books/covers/regression_test_draft_with_content_cover.png

# Real customer PII (name/email/company/description) and auth secrets --
# unlike this repo's internal business data (decisions.jsonl, finance_data.json,
# etc., which ARE committed by convention), these must never land in git.
# Customer Platform Round 1 (2026-07-29) audit finding: customer_requests.jsonl/
# support_tickets.jsonl/consultation_log.jsonl/customer_pipeline_state.json were
# never added here even though the code that writes them has existed since
# ADR-129/130 (2026-07-25) -- fixed now, before any real request data exists.
data/customer_accounts.json
data/customer_requests.jsonl
data/support_tickets.jsonl
data/consultation_log.jsonl
data/customer_pipeline_state.json
data/customer_reviews.jsonl
data/.customer_session_secret
# Internal Market Validation System (2026-08-14): real validation
# responses carry optional contact PII (email/contact), so the ledger
# must never land in git -- same customer-PII rule as the rows above.
data/validation_responses.jsonl

# Final Executive Directive (2026-07-29): pure ephemeral tick run-state,
# same .factory_loop.lock precedent above -- data/generated_business_
# blueprints.jsonl (the real, meaningful append-only ledger these markers
# gate) IS committed by the same convention as decisions.jsonl/etc.
data/.knowledge_graph_daily_marker
data/.business_blueprint_daily_marker
# Disposable rebuild cache -- knowledge_graph.build.build_graph() derives
# this deterministically from already-tracked real ledgers (decisions.jsonl,
# market_intelligence_analyses.jsonl, sales_ledger.jsonl, ai_cost_log.jsonl);
# mission_control_api.py's own _knowledge_graph() docstring already called
# save_snapshot()'s output "a disposable on-disk copy".
data/knowledge_graph_snapshot.json
# Security P1 C3 (2026-08-18): integrity_monitor.py's own baseline state
# (hashes + line counts only, no ledger content) -- a disposable derived
# cache, advanced on every clean check, same precedent as the knowledge
# graph snapshot above. Never a ledger itself.
data/ledger_integrity_baseline.json
# Security P1 item 5 (2026-08-18): Mission Control auth audit ledger --
# records who-tried-when (at/event/ip only, never passwords or tokens).
# Internal security metadata, not business data; gitignored so enabling
# it never risks a secret commit. AUTH_AUDIT_FILE can point it elsewhere.
data/auth_audit.jsonl
